  <item>
    <title>Lubbock: data center moratorium — Proposed</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/lubbock-tx</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-lubbock-tx</guid>
    <pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>Citizen petition for an 18-month moratorium on hyperscale data centers; 3,900+ verified signatures. Council accepted the petition Aug 25. On Sep 8 council passed a non-binding resolution stating large-scale data centers will not be developed until regulations are adopted; the formal 18-month moratorium petition vote was deferred to later in September. If council rejects, organizers can put it on the ballot (May 2027 at earliest)</description>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>Austin County: data center moratorium — Enacted</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/austin-county-tx</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-austin-county-tx</guid>
    <pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>Commissioners unanimously approved a countywide moratorium on AI data centers and battery energy storage systems in unincorporated areas. Developers must submit equipment audits and sworn compliance certifications.</description>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>Athens: data center moratorium — Enacted</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/athens-tx</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-athens-tx</guid>
    <pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>City Council voted 3-2 to permanently ban data centers within city limits. Defines data center as any facility over 500 sq ft used primarily to house servers. Not a moratorium -- a standing zoning ban.</description>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>Tom Green County: data center moratorium — Rejected</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/tom-green-county-tx</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-tom-green-county-tx</guid>
    <pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>Commissioners rejected a 12-month moratorium on large-scale data centers, BESS, and power generation in Precinct 4; cited legal risk after Hill County&#x27;s moratorium drew a $100M federal lawsuit.</description>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>Hood County: data center moratorium — Rejected</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/hood-county-tx</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-hood-county-tx</guid>
    <pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>Commissioners voted down a proposed moratorium 3-2. State Sen. Bettencourt warned county lacked legal authority. County sought AG opinion on whether it could impose restrictions.</description>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>Forney: data center moratorium — Proposed</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/forney-tx</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-forney-tx</guid>
    <pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>Council directed staff to amend zoning to prohibit data centers in all districts -- effectively a proposed citywide ban. Escalation from April 2026 regulations requiring 5,000-ft setbacks.</description>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>Lewisville: data center moratorium — Enacted</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/lewisville-tx</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-lewisville-tx</guid>
    <pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>Council voted unanimously to require Special Use Permit for data centers; banned in all residential areas. Each proposal needs two public hearings.</description>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>El Paso: data center moratorium — Enacted</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/el-paso-tx</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-el-paso-tx</guid>
    <pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>Council unanimously approved data center policy: 300-ft buffer from residential/ecological sites, special use permit, no more tax breaks. Developers must submit resource use, emissions, noise, and water treatment plans.</description>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>Corpus Christi: data center moratorium — Proposed</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/corpus-christi-tx</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-corpus-christi-tx</guid>
    <pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>Council directed staff to pursue prohibiting data centers in all zoning districts; requires data centers to fully fund own infrastructure. Drought context: severe water crisis threatening city reservoirs.</description>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>Milam County: data center moratorium — Enacted</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/milam-county-tx</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-milam-county-tx</guid>
    <pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>Resolution calling for stricter statewide standards on data centers: public disclosure of electrical demand, water consumption, cooling technologies, and infrastructure impact. Non-binding.</description>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>Princeton: data center moratorium — Enacted</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/princeton-tx</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-princeton-tx</guid>
    <pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>City amended regulations to require a Specific Use Permit for data centers, updated definitions, and established per-project public review.</description>
  </item>
  <item>
    <title>Mesquite: data center moratorium — Proposed</title>
    <link>https://aigridwatch.com/communities/mesquite-tx</link>
    <guid isPermaLink="false">mora-mesquite-tx</guid>
    <pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
    <description>Proposed framework: 5-acre min lot, 65 dB noise limit, banned in residential/agricultural/commercial districts. Staff recommended ordinance over moratorium. Not yet enacted.</description>
  </item>
